      "writtenOn": "2025-11-14T20:09:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So generally, for this function, I think we are imagining something more on the line of:\n\n```\nauto AddCaps(std::span\u003cwgpu::TextureFormat\u003e formats, Cap caps,\n             Feature feature \u003d Feature::InvalidEnum) {\n  bool supported \u003d \n    feature \u003d\u003d Feature::InvalidEnum || device-\u003eHasFeature(feature);\n    \n  for (auto format : formats) {\n    Format\u0026 format \u003d /* look up from the table */ \n \n    if (supported) {\n      format.caps ||\u003d caps;\n      // Set unsupportedReason \u003d supported.\n    } else {\n      if (format.caps \u003d\u003d Cap::None) {\n        // Set unsupportedReason \u003d RequiresFeature{feature}.\n      }\n    }\n}\n\n// Add all format caps that apply in compat mode:\nAddCaps(kSomeFormatAlwaysSupported, Cap::A | Cap::B);\n\n// Handle additional core caps:\nif (core) {\n  AddCaps({kSomeFormatAlwaysSupported, kFormatCoreOnly}, Cap::A | Cap::C);\n} else {\n  ExplainUnsupported(kFormatCoreOnly, CompatibilityMode{});\n}\n\n// For each feature add the respective capabilities:\n\n// Feature::Float32Blendable\nAddCaps({wgpu::TextureFormat::R32Float,\n         wgpu::TextureFormat::RG32Float,\n         wgpu::TextureFormat::RGBA32Float},\n        Cap::Blendable,\n        Feature::Float32Blendable);\n...\n\n// Iterate all the formats and ensure that they have at least \n// one cap or an unsupported reason.\n```",
